  "review": {
    "review": "The hero died from a skeleton's bone explosion: decision 2254 targets the adjacent skeleton with 2 HP, and accepted transition line 6723 records zero HP; the recorded death message confirms the cause. Earlier resource ordering contributed to the vulnerability. The hero entered the shop starving at 6 HP. Known rations were visible by decision 2183, but bags and scrolls outranked food. At decision 2192, a reachable 100-gold ration was available with 798 gold and no safe carried food, yet the bot pursued scrolls and did not buy food until decision 2203. The proposed focused correction prioritizes known rations while already starving without safe food, preserving curse-removal priority, route restrictions and purchase confirmation. An isolated original-source selector probe matches decision 2192; the candidate selects the admitted food approach instead. This is not a full runtime-memory reconstruction or evidence that the changed choice prevents death. The new regression fails on original policy with two expected assertions and passes on the candidate; the full suite passes 1881 tests with four skips. The terminal spacing problem and earlier resource depletion remain outside this repair.",
    "learnings": "When already starving without safe carried food, buy an observed, affordable ration before optional shop supplies. Raw mystery meat is not safe carried food. Keep existing movement and purchase checks; choosing food does not prove acquisition or survival."
  },
